🟡 **Medium** `reducers/license_management.ts:126`

When `getLicense(state)` returns `null`, `getLicenseType(state)` returns `undefined`, which causes `shouldShowRequestTrialExtension` to incorrectly return `true`. The condition `(type !== 'platinum' && type !== 'enterprise')` evaluates to `true` when `type` is `undefined`, so the "request trial extension" UI may appear even when no license data exists. Consider adding a guard to return `false` when `type` is `undefined`.

```diff
 export const shouldShowRequestTrialExtension = (state: LicenseManagementState) => {
+  const type = getLicenseType(state);
+  if (!type) {
+    return false;
+  }
   if (state.trialStatus.canStartTrial) {
     return false;
   }
-  const type = getLicenseType(state);
   return (type !== 'platinum' && type !== 'enterprise') || isExpired(state);
 };
```


